{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '326,375p' pose-mcp/internal/cli/scaffold.go\"","aggregated_output":"func cmdNewRoadmap(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n\tlocale := cliLocaleValue()\n\tif len(args) != 1 || !scaffoldSlug.MatchString(args[0]) {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Usage: pose new-roadmap <roadmap-slug>\", \"Uso: pose new-roadmap <roadmap-slug>\"))\n\t\treturn 2\n\t}\n\tslug := args[0]\n\ttemplatePath := filepath.Join(root, \".pose\", \"templates\", \"roadmap.md\")\n\ttemplate, err := os.ReadFile(templatePath)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: template not found: %s\\n\", \"Erro: template ausente: %s\\n\"), templatePath)\n\t\treturn 2\n\t}\n\tpath := filepath.Join(root, \".pose\", \"roadmaps\", slug+\".md\")\n\tif _, err := os.Stat(path); err == nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: roadmap already exists: %s\\n\", \"Erro: roadmap já existe: %s\\n\"), path)\n\t\treturn 1\n\t}\n\tcontent := strings.ReplaceAll(string(template), \"<roadmap-slug>\", slug)\n\tcontent = strings.ReplaceAll(content, \"<YYYY-MM-DD>\", time.Now().UTC().Format(\"2006-01-02\"))\n\tcontent = strings.ReplaceAll(content, \"<created_at>\", time.Now().UTC().Format(\"2006-01-02\"))\n\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(path), 0o755); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: creating roadmap: %v\\n\", \"Erro: criar roadmap: %v\\n\"), err)\n\t\treturn 1\n\t}\n\tif err := os.WriteFile(path, []byte(content), 0o644); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: writing roadmap: %v\\n\", \"Erro: escrever roadmap: %v\\n\"), err)\n\t\treturn 1\n\t}\n\tfmt.Fprintf(stdout, cliText(locale, \"Roadmap created: %s (status: draft)\\n\", \"Roadmap criado: %s (status: draft)\\n\"), path)\n\treturn 0\n}\n\n// applySpecSurface records the surface in the frontmatter and, for minimal,\n// drops what a small change does not need (spec\n// pose-progressive-spec-surface): the planner-local Tasks section and the\n// Final Report subsections `pose specs facts` derives. Intent, requirements,\n// artifacts, the requirement trace and follow-ups stay.\nvar templateSurfaceKey = regexp.MustCompile(`(?m)^surface:[^\\n]*$`)\n\nfunc applySpecSurface(content, surface string) string {\n\t// The template already carries a commented `surface:` key; fill it rather\n\t// than adding a second one (spec pose-spec-surface-single-key).\n\tif loc := templateSurfaceKey.FindStringIndex(content); loc != nil {\n\t\tcontent = content[:loc[0]] + \"surface: \" + surface + content[loc[1]:]\n\t} else {\n\t\tcontent = strings.Replace(content, \"\\ntask_type:\", \"\\nsurface: \"+surface+\"\\ntask_type:\", 1)\n\t}\n\tif surface != pose.SpecSurfaceMinimal {\n\t\treturn content\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '234,255p' .pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '234,255p' .pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\"","aggregated_output":"## Capacity recalibration of captured input bytes (D10) — 2026-11-13\n\nClosing spec `pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit`, `pose index` in a\nfresh clone and then in the maintainer checkout refused the pose-dist corpus:\n`index.delivery-integrity` exceeded the captured-input budget and\n`index.generate` was left without a complete observation. Measured with a Git\nshim on the real builder: the change sets of every spec read `git show\n--binary` for 2,451 distinct trailer commits, 492 MB of Git output in the\ncapture (the final audit reads it again under its own budget), plus the file\ninputs of the generation, so the operation needed more than 512 MiB. Nothing\nwas truncated; the refusal was correct. Raise the captured-input budget to\n1 GiB, for capture and audit alike, and keep every other limit, including the\n512 MiB executable-hash bound of D9. Observations retain their bytes, so the\noperation may now hold up to 1 GiB of captured input in memory. This\nrecalibration buys headroom, not a scaling property: the corpus grows with\nevery attributed commit. The structural fix, retaining only a digest for pure\nreads of immutable Git objects whose bytes a producer only hashes, is a\nfollow-up of that spec, and a further raise again requires a measured\nreassessment.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
