{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_114","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '2850,2995p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\"","aggregated_output":"\t\t\t// a pass.\n\t\t\tif requiresEvidence {\n\t\t\t\tif len(criterion.EvidenceClasses) > 0 {\n\t\t\t\t\treturn ReviewAttestation{}, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: criterion %s requires evidence class %s and bundle %s seals none; run the check, or record the criterion as not-applicable with a rationale using `pose review attest`\", criterion.ID, strings.Join(criterion.EvidenceClasses, \"|\"), bundleID)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\treturn ReviewAttestation{}, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: criterion %s has no evidence in bundle %s; run a check, or record the criterion as not-applicable with a rationale using `pose review attest`\", criterion.ID, bundleID)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\trationale := \"the scope carries no delivery target, so no validation evidence is collected for it\"\n\t\t\tif len(criterion.EvidenceClasses) > 0 {\n\t\t\t\trationale = \"the scope carries no delivery target, so no evidence of class \" + strings.Join(criterion.EvidenceClasses, \"|\") + \" is collected for it\"\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tcriteria = append(criteria, ReviewCriterion{\n\t\t\t\tID:          criterion.ID,\n\t\t\t\tDisposition: \"not-applicable\",\n\t\t\t\tRationale:   rationale,\n\t\t\t})\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tevidenceRefs = append(evidenceRefs, critEvidence)\n\t\tcriteria = append(criteria, ReviewCriterion{\n\t\t\tID:          criterion.ID,\n\t\t\tDisposition: \"passed\",\n\t\t\tEvidence:    critEvidence,\n\t\t})\n\t}\n\tevidenceRefs = uniqueSorted(evidenceRefs)\n\n\ttools := make([]ReviewToolDisposition, 0, len(bundle.Payload.Plan.Tools))\n\tfor _, tool := range bundle.Payload.Plan.Tools {\n\t\tdisposition := ReviewToolDisposition{\n\t\t\tID:        tool.ID,\n\t\t\tComponent: tool.Component,\n\t\t}\n\t\tif containsFold(tool.Preconditions, \"review-complete\") {\n\t\t\tdisposition.Disposition = \"deferred\"\n\t\t\tdisposition.Rationale = \"post-review gate\"\n\t\t} else if tool.ProducerCoverage == \"none\" {\n\t\t\t// A fact the engine computed from the matrix, not a judgment: this\n\t\t\t// component declares that it runs no check, so nothing can produce\n\t\t\t// what the tool asks for. Preparing it here is what keeps the\n\t\t\t// reviewer from having to cite another component's result.\n\t\t\tdisposition.Disposition = \"not-used\"\n\t\t\tdisposition.Rationale = \"the validation matrix declares this component runs no check, so no producer can emit evidence of class \" + strings.Join(tool.EvidenceClasses, \"|\")\n\t\t} else if tool.Requiredness == \"recommended\" {\n\t\t\tdisposition.Disposition = \"not-used\"\n\t\t\tdisposition.Rationale = \"not used during automated attestation\"\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\ttoolEv := \"\"\n\t\t\ttoolComponents := []string{}\n\t\t\tif tool.Component != \"\" {\n\t\t\t\ttoolComponents = append(toolComponents, tool.Component)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\ttoolEv = pickScoped(tool.EvidenceClasses, toolComponents)\n\t\t\tif toolEv == \"\" && len(tool.EvidenceClasses) == 0 {\n\t\t\t\t// A tool that declares no evidence class does not report a\n\t\t\t\t// validation result at all — `artifact-check` and `review-check`\n\t\t\t\t// are POSE commands, and what supports their disposition is that\n\t\t\t\t// the command ran. Naming the tool is a real reference to that;\n\t\t\t\t// reaching for an unrelated sealed result, as this used to, said\n\t\t\t\t// nothing about whether the tool ran.\n\t\t\t\ttoolEv = \"check:\" + tool.ID\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif toolEv == \"\" {\n\t\t\t\t// The same invention the criteria path stopped doing one spec\n\t\t\t\t// ago, on the other half of the attestation: `validation:auto-\n\t\t\t\t// attest`, `<class>:auto-attest`, `docs:auto-attest` — none of\n\t\t\t\t// them pointing at anything, and nothing downstream checking.\n\t\t\t\t// The distinction between a judged review and a stamped one\n\t\t\t\t// does not survive one half of it being fabricated.\n\t\t\t\tif requiresEvidence {\n\t\t\t\t\tif len(tool.EvidenceClasses) > 0 {\n\t\t\t\t\t\treturn ReviewAttestation{}, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review tool %s requires evidence class %s and bundle %s seals none; run the tool, or record its disposition with `pose review attest --tool`\", tool.ID, strings.Join(tool.EvidenceClasses, \"|\"), bundleID)\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\treturn ReviewAttestation{}, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review tool %s has no evidence in bundle %s; run the tool, or record its disposition with `pose review attest --tool`\", tool.ID, bundleID)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t// `deferred`, not `not-used`: a required tool recorded not-used\n\t\t\t\t// is a blocker whatever the reason, while a deferral is the\n\t\t\t\t// disposition the engine already accepts for a tool whose\n\t\t\t\t// precondition this scope cannot meet.\n\t\t\t\tdisposition.Disposition = \"deferred\"\n\t\t\t\tdisposition.Rationale = \"the scope carries no delivery target, so no evidence this tool reports is collected for it\"\n\t\t\t\ttools = append(tools, disposition)\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tdisposition.Disposition = \"passed\"\n\t\t\tdisposition.Evidence = toolEv\n\t\t}\n\t\ttools = append(tools, disposition)\n\t}\n\n\tdecision := \"approved\"\n\tif len(pending) > 0 {\n\t\t// A preparation that still owes answers is not an approval waiting to\n\t\t// be written. Naming the decision `changes-requested` keeps the object\n\t\t// honest if anything persists it anyway: the verifier refuses it, which\n\t\t// is the correct outcome for a review nobody finished.\n\t\tdecision = \"changes-requested\"\n\t}\n\tatt := ReviewAttestation{\n\t\tBundleID:     bundle.BundleID,\n\t\tBundleDigest: bundle.BundleDigest,\n\t\tReviewer:     reviewer,\n\t\tDecision:     decision,\n\t\tCriteria:     criteria,\n\t\tTools:        tools,\n\t\tEvidenceRefs: evidenceRefs,\n\t\tFindings:     []ReviewFinding{},\n\t}\n\tsort.Slice(pending, func(i, j int) bool { return pending[i].Criterion < pending[j].Criterion })\n\treturn att, pending, nil\n}\n\n// RecordReviewAttestation appends an immutable decision for one sealed bundle.\nfunc (s Store) RecordReviewAttestation(att ReviewAttestation, now time.Time) (ReviewAttestation, error) {\n\tvar result ReviewAttestation\n\terr := s.withReviewAttestationWriteGuard(\"review.attestation.record\", att, func(guarded Store) error {\n\t\tvar err error\n\t\tresult, err = guarded.recordReviewAttestation(att, now, false)\n\t\treturn err\n\t})\n\treturn result, err\n}\n\nfunc (s Store) recordReviewAttestation(att ReviewAttestation, now time.Time, signed bool) (ReviewAttestation, error) {\n\tbundle, err := s.LoadReviewBundle(att.BundleID)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn ReviewAttestation{}, err\n\t}\n\tpolicy, _, err := s.loadReviewPolicy()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn ReviewAttestation{}, err\n\t}\n\tif policy.RequireSignedAttestations && !signed {\n\t\treturn ReviewAttestation{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review policy requires a trusted signed attestation envelope\")\n\t}\n\tatt, err = completeReviewAttestation(bundle, att, now)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn ReviewAttestation{}, err\n\t}\n\t// The approval preflight runs here, in the one writer every channel shares,\n\t// before anything is written: an approval the verifier would reject is\n\t// refused, not recorded and rejected later (spec\n\t// pose-review-approval-domain-preflight).\n\tif blockers := s.reviewApprovalAdmissionBlockers(bundle, att, now); len(blockers) > 0 {\n\t\treturn ReviewAttestation{}, &ReviewApprovalRefusal{BundleID: bundle.BundleID, Blockers: blockers}\n\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_115","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nFour medium blockers remain: historical-roadmap misclassification, an invalid template default, incorrect Markdown fence handling, and whitespace-sensitive association keys. R11-N39 is partial; the other three prior findings are fixed.\n\nFocused tests, artifact-check, surface-check, and diff hygiene passed. Both full validation reruns failed: the module run encountered HTTP 403 fetching published releases; the global run also exceeded its 600-second unit-test limit. Extra Go probes could not start in the read-only sandbox. The findings below rest on source traces.\n\nApplied the review workflow and backend-go, security, documentation-style, delivery-evidence, and knowledge-governance rules. The repository remains unchanged; no attestation was recorded.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N42\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\",\n      \"line\": 720,\n      \"summary\": \"Require evidence that a roadmap actually closed before adoption before classifying it as historical. closeoutScopeHistorical accepts the current legacy enabled/cutoff shortcut or any recorded bundle approval, without checking whether that bundle sealed CloseoutReview. A roadmap approved under schema 5 and subsequently marked done without a receipt therefore becomes historical: closeoutReviewGate returns nil, getCloseoutState does not require a receipt, and CLI close can report already-satisfied. The enabled=false branch can also suppress adopted always and recorded negative reviews on a done roadmap. This violates R2/R4/R5 and the prospective-history contract. Apply the sealed pre-adoption-plan distinction used by milestoneClosedBeforeAdoption and cover both post-adoption approval and disabled-policy cases.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N43\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \".pose/templates/roadmap.md\",\n      \"line\": 6,\n      \"summary\": \"Emit a valid optional association default. The new template writes adrs: followed only by an inline explanatory comment; the distributed scaffold has the same line. cmdNewRoadmap preserves it, but associationList reads the raw comment as the value and rejects it as outside a list. Filling the required roadmap fields while leaving this optional field untouched consequently makes when-justified evaluation unknown and prevents close. Omit the optional declaration or emit a parseable empty list with its explanation on a separate comment line, and exercise the generated template through the evaluator.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N44\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\",\n      \"line\": 88,\n      \"summary\": \"Preserve the complete Markdown fence delimiter and validate its closing syntax. markdownWithoutCode truncates every opener to three characters. For valid Markdown consisting of an opening four-backtick fence, a literal three-backtick line inside it, example text, the closing four-backtick fence, and then a real ADR link, the three-backtick line prematurely closes this filter's fence and the real closing delimiter opens another one. The actual association is discarded without a diagnostic. A two-member roadmap whose sole ADR association is that link consequently receives Known=true and Required=false under when-justified, violating R3. Cover longer fences and real links following them.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N45\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\",\n      \"line\": 112,\n      \"summary\": \"Normalize association keys consistently with SplitFrontmatter before tracking their presence and duplicates. SplitFrontmatter splits at the colon and trims the key, whereas associationList recognizes only a literal unindented key followed immediately by a colon. Thus adrs : [adr:decision.md], or the equivalent roadmaps declaration, is silently absent here despite being recognized by the repository's frontmatter reader. With two canonical members and no other association, when-justified grants an exemption without a diagnostic. Differently spaced duplicate keys also escape duplicate detection. This is the remaining R11-N39 gap: recognize normalized keys and reject ambiguity before proving association absence.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R11-N38\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:2747 restricts the declaredUnreviewed exception to !closeoutAdopted. go test ./internal/pose -run '^TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundTwelve$' -count=1 -v passed, including the legacy-attempt child-rejection subtest without skipping.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R11-N39\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go:119 rejects repeated literal keys; lines 123-137 reject missing values, nonlists and empty items. RoundTwelve association-declaration tests passed. However line 112 does not normalize keys as SplitFrontmatter does at pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go:593, leaving the whitespace and duplicate-key bypass reported as N45.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R11-N40\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go:45 applies markdownWithoutCode. The RoundTwelve fenced, tilde, inline-code and comment regression cases all passed. N44 reports a distinct undercount caused by longer fence delimiters.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R11-N41\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"git diff --check 8e3009b2c7305cd94500009875ddc1b7880d8331 38e6d16ae90f6e8266c56d2e12b2465269fdb4ac exited 0 with no output.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed R1-R7, decisions D1/D2, the accepted ADR, changed implementation, schemas, templates and English/Portuguese scaffold documentation. Traced policy parsing and adoption, protected baseline and mandatory-human enforcement, canonical members and transfers, both ADR association directions, voluntary-review vetoes, receipts and interrupted-close recovery. Swept CLI close, review-check, review verification, review-plan, closeout state/MCP, reached and nextCloses, roadmap acceptance checks, obligations/attention, readiness, portfolio dependencies, federated acceptance and doctor. Examined bounded reads, operation-scoped state, writer guards and immutable publication. Ran the full TestCloseoutReviewPolicy prefix across domain/CLI/MCP and the verbose RoundTwelve regressions; all passed. Ran artifact-check, surface-check, suggest-review, diff hygiene and both required validate commands. Validation reruns failed as detailed in tools. Additional in-memory Go probes could not start because the sandbox refused a temporary build directory; the new findings are established by source traces. A read-only Python trace confirmed the template value, key-normalization disagreement and longer-fence state transitions. Final git status was clean. No repository edits, attestation, contribution staging or upstream submission occurred.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-41a20ef8e08d77e3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared implementer claims with the spec, accepted ADR, source and executed checks. Distinguished sealed successful validation from the failed fresh reruns and source-established defects from the blocked extra probes. Historical classification is an implementation defect in N42, not an accepted assumption; no new residual risk is accepted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected copied operation-local traversal state, root guards, publication revalidation, ExpectAbsent receipt publication and intent/status/receipt ordering. Found no new concurrent-access or overwrite defect within the participating-writer contract.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N43\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The shipped roadmap producer emits an optional field that the new runtime rejects.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N45\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Recognized association-key spellings can disappear without an unknown-input diagnostic.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N42\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The incorrect historical classification propagates through closeout, reached/dependency projections and CLI close.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N45\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The association declaration is silently treated as absent, so consumers receive a known exemption instead of actionable missing-knowledge context.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N42\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The historical compatibility exception also admits closures made after adoption and can re-enable legacy shortcuts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N42\",\n      \"rationale\": \"An adopted roadmap can become terminal without its required explicit-close receipt.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-41a20ef8e08d77e3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The accepted design separates lifecycle close from aggregate review, uses deterministic canonical-member/ADR thresholds, and centralizes policy decisions while preserving member review and vetoes. Schema 5 makes adoption explicit and receipts provide a distinct terminal marker. The findings concern implementation gaps in these decisions.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-3ce6ee69\",\n          \"basis\": \"D2\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The technical-plan reconciliation explicitly includes the measured D10 read-view capacity adjustment needed by governance reads supporting closeout. The amendment retains a finite bound and records the digest-only scaling follow-up.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-607ff681\",\n          \"basis\": \"R3\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The roadmap template adds the explicit ADR association metadata consumed by when-justified. Its invalid empty default is N43.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-ec2d86f4\",\n          \"basis\": \"R1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The new accepted ADR records policy location, defaults, deterministic modes, explicit close, veto preservation and historical compatibility.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N43\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The installed and distributed roadmap templates disagree with the strict runtime declaration grammar.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N43\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Leaving the documented optional association field untouched blocks a normally populated generated roadmap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N44\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R3 is not satisfied for valid Markdown containing longer fences; N42 also violates the explicit-close and prospective-history requirements.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reviewed artifacts implement the approved schema/evaluator/receipt/configuration/projection scope. The budget adjustment is explicitly reconciled in the technical plan and measured ADR amendment. No unrelated refactor or new global ADR identity/configuration framework was introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N45\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Association-input normalization can lower an aggregate's review obligation without reporting unknown authority inputs. N42 supplies another route around the adopted gate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-41a20ef8e08d77e3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the implementation with a boolean toggle or projection-only exemption. Neither supplies the required middle mode, explicit-close marker and historical semantics. Reusing the capability catalog, resolver and publication guards is proportionate; owner-local ADR inventory avoids speculative global discovery. Remote backlink requirements would invalidate that boundary. The 1 GiB adjustment buys measured headroom rather than scalability, as the ADR and spec follow-up explicitly disclose.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran the required command; exit 0. It emitted warning orphan diagnostics for governed tracked paths without provenance claims, rather than failing the gate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-41a20ef8e08d77e3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used sealed structural evidence and direct spec/ADR/source inspection without regenerating assessment artifacts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used the supplied component scope, sealed evidence and direct source inspection; did not refresh writing assessment state.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Avoided the writing assessment under the immutable-checkout boundary. Traced CLI, Store, MCP, dependency and federation consumers directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected changed code, marker search results and the spec's recorded follow-ups without writing debt reports.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-terminal-verification-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion gate requires POSE to verify and record this review conclusion first.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred until POSE records the verified review conclusion; this reviewer must not attest.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Exit 0; selected the review workflow and backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict; exit 0: surface.targets=1, surface.results=213, surface.findings=0. Sealed composition evidence: integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration. Sealed reachability evidence: reachability:pose-mcp/go/closeout-plan-reachability.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose validate --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Fresh invocation exited 1: 213 steps, 211 pass, 1 fail, 1 error. The pose-mcp unit check timed out after 600 seconds. This is not reported as a successful rerun; the bundle's sealed successful validation remains separate historical evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Fresh invocation exited 1: 210 steps, 209 pass, 1 fail. Unit tests, build, vet and closeout-review-policy integration passed. install-and-upgrade-journeys-integration failed at TestJourneysInstallAndUpgradeFromThePublishedRelease because curl received HTTP 403 while listing published releases. That external prerequisite prevents claiming a successful fresh component validation; it does not establish another scoped code defect.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
